{"id": "EUVD-2026-101454", "enisaUuid": "0ded16f6-ab90-3455-b99c-74f3747eef47", "description": "An Incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs vulnerability in the routing protocol daemon (rpd) of Juniper Networks Junos OS and Junos OS Evolved allows an unauthenticated, adjacent attacker to cause a Denial-of-Service (DoS).\n\nWhen in a BGP traffic engineering scenario a specific, valid, optional, non-transitive BGP update is received over an established BGP session, RPD crashes and automatically restarts, which leads to traffic impact until routing has reconverged.\n\nThis issue affects:\nJunos OS:\n\n\n  *  All versions before 23.2R2-S6;\n  *  23.4 versions before 23.4R2-S7;\n  *  24.2 versions before 24.2R2-S4;\n  *  24.4 versions before 24.4R2-S4;\n  *  25.2 versions before 25.2R1-S2, 25.2R2;\n\n\n\nJunos OS Evolved:\n  *  All versions before 23.2R2-S6-EVO;\n  *  23.4 versions before 23.4R2-S8.11-EVO;\n  *  24.2 versions before 24.2R2-S4-EVO;\n  *  24.4 versions before 24.4R2-S5-EVO;\n  *  25.2 versions before 25.2R1-S2-EVO, 25.2R2-EVO;", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T16:23:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T20:26:06", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L/AU:Y/R:A/RE:M", "references": ["https://supportportal.juniper.net/JSA112168"], "aliases": ["GHSA-457r-m358-cv7v", "CVE-2026-102087"], "assigner": "juniper", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f5744a7-65ba-3cc4-b372-10e5c93c3f2f", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "24.2 <24.2R2-S4-EVO"}, {"id": "2125d376-ca0a-3f43-94dd-7598d1e5571b", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "24.2 <24.2R2-S4"}, {"id": "7c4bdf38-8574-3f8f-9485-e1cbdfa4b452", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "23.4 <23.4R2-S7"}, {"id": "81077f11-f974-38f1-8a69-0fc2cb3af07e", "product": {"nam